 "notes": [
  "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Acromag_961_962EN_Module_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/961_962EN_MODBUS_EXTRACT.pdf).",
  "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
  "Only 18 of the 139 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
  "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
  "Names use the letter O for zero in channel 00/01 (CHOO, CHOI) as printed."
 ],
